{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310831,"nonce":"ex//47t/bQB2GwYWaU44oETCeYo=","title":"Known issues preventing DeltaBlue benchmark from running — drop tracking, temp freeing, and pop() boxing","message":"DeltaBlue benchmark (compiler/benchmarks/src/deltablue.hx) cannot run yet. Expected output: `total: 14065400`.\n\n\n1. **Virtual dispatch from constructors**: Pre-registration override fix in ast_lowering.rs\n2. **`func().field = value` heap corruption**: FieldAccess temp registration only for New, not Call\n3. **Variable alias premature free**: `var current = n1` ownership transfer in Let handler\n4. **While loop use-after-free**: Assign handler no longer treats Call results as owned allocations\n\n\n**Pattern**: `var c = todo.pop()` where todo is `Array\u003cConstraint\u003e`.\n**Why**: pop() returns `Null\u003cT\u003e` (boxed DynamicValue*). For class types, the boxed return needs unboxing to get the raw pointer. The unboxing path for class pointers from pop/shift is broken.\n**Workaround**: Use `var c = todo[todo.length - 1]; todo.splice(todo.length - 1, 1);` instead of `pop()`.\n**How to apply**: Fix the `Null\u003cT\u003e` unboxing for class-type array pop/shift in the MIR wrapper or runtime.\n\n**Pattern**: `while (todo.length \u003e 0) { todo = todo.slice(0, todo.length - 1); ... }`\n**Why**: Variable reassignment inside while loop creates phi node at loop header. The phi merges initial value and slice result. The phi node gives back the wrong value (original array instead of sliced), causing infinite loop.\n**Workaround**: Use `todo.splice(todo.length - 1, 1)` (mutates in place) instead of reassignment.\n**How to apply**: Fix phi node handling for array/pointer variable reassignment in while loops (lower_while_loop in hir_to_mir.rs).\n\n**Pattern**: `out.determinedBy = this` in non-override methods works, but `c.output().mark = mark` still generates a read-back FieldAccess that calls output() twice.\n**Why**: HIR wraps assignment in a Block that reads back the assigned value (expression-position assignment). The read-back evaluates `c.output()` a second time.\n**Workaround**: Use `var cOut = c.output(); cOut.mark = mark;` instead.\n**How to apply**: Either suppress the read-back Block for void-context assignments, or ensure the read-back doesn't cause side effects.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_deltablue_blockers` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}